    {
      "id": "-_MppE2cYtV6o3GkfmWsH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1801.4010690403272,
      "y": 809.7934729744371,
      "width": 1029.6593017578125,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 720518550,
      "version": 101,
      "versionNonce": 1229636694,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781730349712,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "***** Component responsibilities ****\n1. UI: \n-- Displays the document and sends events to the rich text editor core.\n2. Rich text editor core: \n-- Holds the document state/model, similar to the core of the rich text editor system design. \n-- Responds to user events by manipulating the underlying document state, which triggers DOM events. \n-- Provides APIs for external modifications of the document state.\n3. Sync engine: \n-- Module responsible for syncing local updates to the server, \nreceiving updates from the server (transforming appropriate operations), and updating the editor core. \nMost of what was discussed above lives in this module.\n---- Local updates buffer: Local operations that have not been sent to the server.\n---- Sent updates buffer: Local operations that have been sent to the server \nbut not yet acknowledged by the server.\n---- Updates log: Revisions that have been committed as part of the document history.4.\n4. Server: WebSocket server that can receive and push updates to the client.\n-- Pending updates: Operations from clients that have not been committed.\n-- Revision log: Operations that have been processed and can give the complete history of the document.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "***** Component responsibilities ****\n1. UI: \n-- Displays the document and sends events to the rich text editor core.\n2. Rich text editor core: \n-- Holds the document state/model, similar to the core of the rich text editor system design. \n-- Responds to user events by manipulating the underlying document state, which triggers DOM events. \n-- Provides APIs for external modifications of the document state.\n3. Sync engine: \n-- Module responsible for syncing local updates to the server, \nreceiving updates from the server (transforming appropriate operations), and updating the editor core. \nMost of what was discussed above lives in this module.\n---- Local updates buffer: Local operations that have not been sent to the server.\n---- Sent updates buffer: Local operations that have been sent to the server \nbut not yet acknowledged by the server.\n---- Updates log: Revisions that have been committed as part of the document history.4.\n4. Server: WebSocket server that can receive and push updates to the client.\n-- Pending updates: Operations from clients that have not been committed.\n-- Revision log: Operations that have been processed and can give the complete history of the document.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
